tlib's BuiltinImporter"] [187 21 "// stderr unbuffered, as CPython's: the banner before the hook's and _pyrepl's imports (queue 298)"] [194 2 "// sys.__interactivehook__ (pymain_run_interactive_hook; queue 298: site's register_readline, the history file)"] [198 2 "// on a terminal, _pyrepl (pymain_run_pyrepl; queue 298): pythonstartup after code (pymain_repl), not on stdin's run"] [199 2 "// (pymain_run_stdin ran the startup file above)"] [206 1 "// mainModuleDefaults gives __main__'s namespace g of a run with no code the names CPython's __main__ starts with"] [207 1 "// (add_main_module, Python/pylifecycle.c): __package__ and __spec__ None, __loader__ BuiltinImporter, each when absent."] [229 1 "// runInteractiveHook is pymain_run_interactive_hook (Modules/main.c; queue 298), before the REPL: sys.__interactivehook__"] [230 1 "// called when sys has one (site's register_readline: readline's or _pyrepl's history file read, its write at exit"] [231 1 "// registered); an error is \"Failed calling sys.__interactivehook__\" and printed, the session going on, but SystemExit,"] [232 1 "// whose status ends the run (exit true), as pymain_err_print."] [237 2 "// site, which CPython imports at start (pyi does not): imported here, before the REPL, so that its main sets the hook"] [238 2 "// (enablerlcompleter, but under -I)"] [262 1 "// runStartup is pymain_run_startup (Modules/main.c; queue 293), before the REPL on stdin when there is no code to run:"] [263 1 "// the file PYTHONSTARTUP names (not under -E or -I) run in __main__'s namespace g as _PyRun_SimpleFileObject runs it,"] [264 1 "// its __file__ set for the run, an error printed (sys.excepthook) and the session going on; SystemExit ends the run"] [265 1 "// with its status (exit true), as PyErr_Print's handle_system_exit; a file that does not open: \"Could not open"] [266 1 "// PYTHONSTARTUP\" and its OSError printed."] [309 1 "// cModeFile is the file bin/pyi python writes -c's code into (queue 220): run as CPython runs -c, its code's file"] [310 1 "// \"<string>\", no __file__, sys.path[0] \"\"."] [313 1 "// mModeFile and stdinModeFile are the files bin/pyi python writes for -m and for a program read from stdin (queue 250)."] [319 1 "// startSafePath is -P (safe_path) as bin/pyi python's command line gave it (PYI_SAFE_PATH: 1 under -P or -I, 0"] [320 1 "// without, read once and removed from the environment as PYI_IGNORE_ENV is); -1 when not run by bin/pyi python (bin/pyi"] [321 1 "// run's programs and the check's driver, whose sys.flags.safe_path is the reference driver's -P)."] [342 1 "// ExecModule runs a module's code object as the module name (its namespace's __name__), returning"] [343 1 "// the module, or the uncaught exception."] [348 1 "// PrintException writes an uncaught exception as CPython's default excepthook does"] [349 1 "// (Lib/traceback.py's format): the chain first (__cause__, else __context__ unless suppressed), each"] [350 1 "// with its traceback (the file, line and function, and the source line when the file reads) and"] [351 1 "// \"Type: text\", a SyntaxError's location and caret, the notes. Carets under expressions are not"] [352 1 "// printed (PY5b: a recorded difference)."] [353 1 "//"] [354 1 "// The text goes to sys.stderr (PyErr_Display's file): the process's standard error while sys.stderr is"] [355 1 "// the one it started with, else the text is written by sys.stderr.write and flushed (support.captured_stderr),"] [356 1 "// nothing when sys.stderr is None or missing, write's errors ignored."] [370 1 "// PrintUncaught is PyErr_Print (Python/pythonrun.c's _PyErr_PrintEx with set_sys_last_vars, queue 223): an uncaught"] [371 1 "// exception, not SystemExit, stored as sys.last_exc, last_type, last_value and last_traceback, then given to"] [372 1 "// sys.excepthook(type, value, traceback); \"sys.excepthook is missing\" and the display when it is absent or None; when"] [373 1 "// the hook raises, \"Error in sys.excepthook:\", that error's display, then \"Original exception was:\" and the original's."] [380 22 "// after the main module's run: the hook runs on the main thread"] [395 2 "// _PyErr_PrintEx's audit (queue 536): a hook's RuntimeError ends the display, another error is unraisable"] [419 1 "// registerCode is run_mod's interactive source (Python/pythonrun.c, queue 223): -c's code and its nested code objects"] [420 1 "// registered by linecache._register_code(code, source, name), so traceback's display shows -c's lines; an error dropped."] [434 1 "// displayByTraceback is _PyErr_Display's first way (Python/pythonrun.c, queue 223): the stdlib's"] [435 1 "// traceback._print_exception_bltin(exc), Lib/traceback.py's display with its caret lines (PEP 657's positions,"] [436 1 "// co_positions), chains, groups and notes; false when the module or its function is missing or the call raised (the"] [437 1 "// error dropped, as PyErr_Clear), the caller then printing the Go display (print_exception_recursive's fallback)."] [438 1 "// Not while traceback itself is being imported or displaying (a second error then printed by the fallback)."] [470 1 "// writeStderr writes text to sys.stderr: in.Stderr when it is the original stream."] [510 4 "// at shutdown CPython's display reads no source (the import of io fails: queue 253)"] [519 1 "// FormatExceptionOnly is traceback.format_exception_only's text: a SyntaxError's location, source"] [520 1 "// line and caret, then \"Type: text\" (the type qualified by its module unless builtins), then the notes."] [525 23 "// traceback's stype: the module unless __main__ or builtins"] [529 3 "// str(exc) (traceback's _safe_string): a class's own __str__"] [609 1 "// RegisterSource gives sourceLine the text of a source that is no file (\"<stdin>\", \"<string>\"): the"] [610 1 "// REPL's statements, as linecache keeps them (PY5e's REQUEST, part 2a). A later text replaces it."] [615 1 "// sourceLine is the stripped text of line n of the file, \"\" when it does not read (linecache)."] [637 1 "// RunModule reads a module's IR (arbace.python.compile's code object as pr-str prints it) and runs it"] [638 1 "// as __main__ with file as __file__, on the process's stdout and stderr; the exit status: 0, 1 for an"] [639 1 "// uncaught exception (its traceback on stderr), SystemExit's code. bin/pyi run calls it."] [640 1 "// mainSourceError is the main file's decoding error as the tokenizer reports a file it reads, the file named"] [641 1 "// (helpers.c's \" in file FILE\", as arbace.python.run/error-answer gives pyi on goi's; queue 284: the compiled"] [642 1 "// launcher's main module, which RunModule decodes): nil when its bytes decode."] [662 1 "// stdinClosed (queue 553): the process was started with descriptor 0 closed (bin/pyi python's PYI_STDIN_CLOSED, which"] [663 1 "// its shell sees before Go's runtime opens /dev/null on a closed 0, 1 or 2 at its start, runtime.checkfds): 0 is"] [664 1 "// closed again before anything runs, so the program sees it closed as CPython's (os.fstat(0) is EBADF, the next"] [665 1 "// open is 0) and sys.stdin is None (create_stdio's is_valid_fd)."] [668 1 "// closeStdinAtStart is stdinClosed's close, the variable read once and removed from the environment."] [681 2 "// SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ ignored at the start, as CPython's init_signals does, not at _signal's first import: a write to a"] [682 2 "// closed pipe is a BrokenPipeError (py-eval-1122: python -m json.tool, which never imports signal, died of SIGPIPE)"] [687 2 "// ir is the compiler's answer when the main module does not compile (queue 223): its SyntaxError raised as"] [688 2 "// compile() raises it and given to sys.excepthook, as CPython's pymain_run_file reports it"] [692 37 "// the reader's warnings, emitted once the interpreter stands (queue 228)"] [697 3 "// the coding spec is a codec of Python's the host has no charset for: decoded and compiled below"] [708 2 "// sys.path[0] as CPython's config computes sys_path_0 (sys is made from configPath on its first u